#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Generate low-correlation regression tasks from the official TabPFN v1 prior.

Data contract
-------------
* The feature core is generated by the official public PriorLabs/TabPFN v1.0.0
  MLP prior at commit ``a9298ae0...`` and its released epoch-42 prior
  configuration.  Every draw is fail-closed on ``is_causal=True`` so the core
  is always generated by the causal SCM branch.  The official target is
  discarded and replaced by the shared sparse-linear regression target.
* Up to 4,096 core features are generated directly by that causal SCM branch.
* Above 4,096 features, each random MLP block samples K uniformly from
  1..min(512, current P), appends 16 independent Gaussian inputs whose variance
  is sampled log-uniformly, and emits 512 candidate features.
* Every candidate is rounded through the exact float16 storage representation
  before testing.  It is compared against every retained feature and against
  its own block on a CUDA device.  Features with |Pearson r| >= the configured
  threshold are dropped, leaving one retained representative.  Thus the final
  stored feature matrix is incrementally and exhaustively certified.
* The response uses the same shared Exp122 sparse-linear target helper as the
  TabICL-v2 half, evaluated on final filtered/permuted float16 X.

The script writes one fixed-shape NPZ stream per worker/part and atomically
updates its manifest after each completed file.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

